    <item>
      <title>Triangulating the Impossible: Why Projective Space Needs Exponential Vertices</title>
      <link>https://www.loomsci.com/pages/2026/09/10/arxiv_2609_10402_triangulating_the_impossible_why_projective_space_needs_exponential_vertices.html</link>
      <description>Every triangulation of real projective d-space demands exponentially many vertices in the square root of the dimension, because a free antipodal mirror cannot be tiled cheaply.</description>
